course: dictionary
lesson: 6198
title: Spotting a mismatch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mismatch is when two things do not fit together or do not match. Look at the words around it to find the clue. «An extra one is called a "blue moon", though it isn't blue, and that mismatch is why every calendar must choose: the Moon, the Sun, or both.» The clue is "though it isn't blue": the name says blue, but the Moon is not blue, so the name and the thing do not match.
explain: Ask yourself what two things are being compared. Here it is the name and the thing it names. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "the gap between the name and the thing is why every calendar must choose". It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Mismatch can also be a noun meaning a one-sided contest, or a verb meaning to put together things that do not match, as in «mismatched socks». Read the whole sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: A mismatch is a situation where two things do not fit together or do not match.
fact: «A mismatch between the picture and the words» means the picture and the words do not agree.
fact: In sport, a mismatch is a contest where one side is much stronger than the other.
fact: In computing, «type mismatch» is an error.
fact: On Odd Socks Day, which is part of Anti-Bullying Week in the UK, people wear «mismatched socks» to celebrate being different.
exercise: «There was a mismatch between the picture and the words.» What does mismatch mean here? | *Two things that do not fit together | A very large picture | Two things that are exactly the same | A short poem
exercise: Sam wears «mismatched socks» on Odd Socks Day. What does mismatched mean? | *Socks that do not match each other | Socks that are very warm | Socks with holes in them | Socks that are brand new
exercise: «Our team lost 12 goals to 0. It was a total mismatch.» What kind of game was it? | A game with no players | *A one-sided contest where one side is much stronger | A tie | A rematch
test: «The match was a total mismatch, with one team scoring ten goals.» What does mismatch mean? | *A contest where one side is much stronger than the other | A kind of weather | Odd socks worn on purpose | Two things that fit together perfectly
test: The computer showed a «type mismatch» error. What is a mismatch here? | A sign that the computer is working well | A kind of game | A new word for a sock | *An error where things do not fit together
exam: Which sentence uses mismatch as a verb? | *She mismatched the socks on purpose | She sorted the socks into neat pairs | The mismatch was a total surprise | He wrote his name at the top of the page
